        "text": "Any activity where you give something to someone in return for something else is a trade. When it comes to financial markets, we typically talk about trading financial assets like stocks, bonds, forex, pairs, options, and cryptocurrencies, among others. Each trader adopts a different strategy according to their risk profile and tolerance. For example, day trading is one of the most common strategies, in which a trader buys and sells financial assets within the same trading day trad. Another option is swing trading, in which trading positions are open for a few days or weeks. Then what is investing? Trading and investing are commonly confused concepts. So what exactly is the difference between the two? The aim of both these activities is similar, but they're somewhat different in their methodologies.",
        "start": 960,
        "end": 50570,
